@page "/tutorial"
@inject NavigationManager Nav

<p style="margin:0 0 20px; font-size:14px; color:var(--n-300); line-height:1.55;">
    A 2-minute, plain-language walkthrough of how your vault keeps things locked — no tech background needed.
</p>

<div class="tl-step">
    <div class="tl-gutter">
        <div class="tl-num">1</div>
        <div class="tl-line"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="gap:6px;">
        <div class="card-title">You get two keys</div>
        <div class="card-body">
            When you create an account, SecureVault generates two keys that belong only to you.
            Think of a mailbox: anyone can drop a letter in, only you have the key to take letters out.
        </div>
        <div class="key-pair">
            <div class="key-card public">
                <h3><span class="pill pill-public">Public</span></h3>
                <p>Share it freely. It is only used to <strong>encrypt</strong> data destined for you.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="key-card private">
                <h3><span class="pill pill-private">Private</span></h3>
                <p>Keep it secret. Only this key can <strong>decrypt</strong> what was locked with your public key.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="tl-step">
    <div class="tl-gutter">
        <div class="tl-num">2</div>
        <div class="tl-line"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="gap:6px;">
        <div class="card-title">Your passphrase guards the private key</div>
        <div class="card-body">
            The private key file on disk is itself encrypted with your master passphrase.
            No passphrase, no access — not even to us. Without it, the file is useless,
            even if someone copies it.
        </div>
        <div class="flow-diagram">
            <span class="flow-box">passphrase</span>
            <span class="arrow">+</span>
            <span class="flow-box">encrypted private key file</span>
            <span class="arrow">=</span>
            <span class="flow-box highlight">unlocked private key</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="tl-step">
    <div class="tl-gutter">
        <div class="tl-num">3</div>
        <div class="tl-line"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="gap:6px;">
        <div class="card-title">Locking a message</div>
        <div class="card-body">
            To send you something private, someone locks it with your <em>public key</em>.
            From that moment only your private key can open it.
        </div>
        <div class="flow-diagram vertical">
            <div class="flow-row">
                <span class="flow-box">plain file</span>
                <span class="arrow">&#10148;</span>
                <span class="flow-box accent">your public key</span>
                <span class="arrow">&#10148;</span>
                <span class="flow-box dark">encrypted .pgp</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flow-row">
                <span class="flow-box dark">encrypted .pgp</span>
                <span class="arrow">&#10148;</span>
                <span class="flow-box accent">your private key + passphrase</span>
                <span class="arrow">&#10148;</span>
                <span class="flow-box">plain file</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="tl-step">
    <div class="tl-gutter">
        <div class="tl-num">4</div>
        <div class="tl-line"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="gap:6px;">
        <div class="card-title">The whole vault is locked too</div>
        <div class="card-body">
            Your passwords, notes and cards are stored as one scrambled blob. On disk it looks
            like meaningless noise until you unlock it. SecureVault uses a hybrid scheme:
            a strong random AES-256 key (encrypted with your PGP public key) does the bulk
            symmetric encryption per field, and the vault as a whole is PGP-wrapped on save.
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="tl-step">
    <div class="tl-gutter">
        <div class="tl-num">5</div>
        <div class="tl-line"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="gap:6px;">
        <div class="card-title">Pick a passphrase you can keep</div>
        <ul class="tip-list">
            <li><strong>Length wins.</strong> A 4-word passphrase like <code>caballo correcto batería grapa</code> is much stronger than <code>P@ss1!</code> and far easier to remember.</li>
            <li><strong>Never reuse it.</strong> If a website you use is breached and you share passphrases, attackers get your vault too.</li>
            <li><strong>Don't write it down digitally.</strong> Pen and paper in a locked drawer is fine.</li>
            <li><strong>It is not recoverable.</strong> If you forget it, nobody — including us — can decrypt your vault.</li>
            <li><strong>Back up the private key file.</strong> Copy <code>private_key.asc</code> to an offline drive.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="tl-step">
    <div class="tl-gutter">
        <div class="tl-num">6</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="gap:6px;">
        <div class="card-title">The key directory</div>
        <div class="card-body">
            To encrypt a file <strong>for someone else</strong>, you need their public key.
            The Key management page lets you import public keys from people you trust so
            you can lock files addressed to them.
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<button class="btn btn-primary btn-block" style="height:44px; margin-top:4px;"
        @onclick='() => Nav.NavigateTo("/keys")'>
    Go to Key management
</button>

<style>
    .key-pair {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 10px;
        margin-top: 8px;
    }
    .key-card {
        padding: 12px;
        border-radius: var(--radius-md);
        background: var(--color-bg);
    }
    .key-card h3 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .key-card p { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--n-300); line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; }

    .flow-diagram {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 8px;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        margin-top: 8px;
    }
    .flow-diagram.vertical { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; gap: 12px; }
    .flow-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .flow-box {
        background: var(--color-bg);
        border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
        padding: 5px 11px;
        font-size: 12px;
        color: var(--color-text);
    }
    .flow-box.highlight { background: var(--a-800); color: var(--a-100); }
    .flow-box.accent { background: var(--a-900); color: var(--a-200); }
    .flow-box.dark { background: var(--n-900); color: var(--n-300); }
    .arrow { color: var(--n-500); font-size: 12px; }

    .tip-list {
        margin: 4px 0 0;
        padding-left: 18px;
        color: var(--n-300);
        line-height: 1.6;
        font-size: 13px;
    }
    .tip-list li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
    .tip-list strong { color: var(--color-text); }
    .tip-list code {
        background: var(--color-bg);
        padding: 1px 6px;
        border-radius: 3px;
        font-size: 11.5px;
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
    }

    @@media (max-width: 600px) {
        .key-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
</style>
